# retro

Follow the project rules in [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) at the repo root. That file is the source of truth; do not contradict it.

In particular:

- **Fidelity first.** Match real hardware behavior, timing, port maps, and status polarity. Cite period sources for quirks. Do not copy another emulator’s shortcuts.
- **Real clocks.** The live page runs at the machine’s actual speed. No visitor-facing turbo. Test-only speed overrides follow the three rules in CLAUDE.md (default off, labelled, opt-in).
- **New machines** are full browser WASM emulators (real CPU, real graphics, real storage), plus GoogleTest and Playwright, wired through `retroweb/Makefile` and `.github/workflows/deploy-emulator.yml`.
- **Copyright.** Do not bundle or fetch ROMs still under active copyright. Ship a labelled free stand-in (test ROM, open BIOS, FreeDOS) and let the user supply originals locally.
- **Arcade cabinets** follow [`.claude/arcade.md`](../../.claude/arcade.md) (high-score persist, hwtest ROMs, shared chips, cabinet chrome).
- **Formatting.** Match the file you are editing. Follow the Formatting section in CLAUDE.md (4-space C++, 2-space JavaScript/TypeScript/HTML/CSS, braces on the same line, the compact theme bootstrap left as-is). Do not reformat unrelated code. Do not add Prettier or clang-format.
- **One working copy.** Always `/Users/chrisgall/code/retro`. Never create git worktrees or sibling folders. For new work, ask Chris where it should go (default `main`; a branch only if he says so). Do not open PRs unless asked.
